  "provenance": [
    "A THIRD-PARTY key, not UPSC. A UPSC question booklet prints no key and the",
    "official one follows the recruitment cycle by roughly a year. This is evidence,",
    "never ground truth: this repo has measured prep-house keys at ~2 errors per 100",
    "on the sibling CDS Mathematics corpus, and on NDA Mathematics 2026-II all three",
    "disagreements with a third-party key resolved AGAINST the key.",
    "",
    "THE HEADING SAYS 'CDS II 2026 - GAT (SET-A)' AND THAT IS A PUBLISHER ERROR.",
    "Recorded rather than silently corrected. CDS has no paper called GAT and no",
    "150-question paper at all (its papers are English 120, GK 120, Elementary",
    "Mathematics 100); GAT is unambiguously NDA Paper II, which is 150 questions.",
    "The filename itself reads NDS_II_2026_GAT_SET_A (NDS being a typo for NDA).",
    "The claim is not settled by that reasoning alone - see the agreement rate in",
    "reconcile-key.ts, which is the empirical test: a key for the WRONG paper scores",
    "near chance (~25%), a key for the right one scores near 90%.",
    "",
    "ONE SERIES COLUMN ONLY. Unlike the Mathematics key, which prints SET-A..SET-D",
    "side by side and where reading the wrong column yields 150 confident WRONG",
    "entries rather than an error, this sheet carries a single Ans. column per",
    "Q.No. pair across five pairs (1-30, 31-60, 61-90, 91-120, 121-150).",
    "",
    "TRANSCRIBED TWICE, by hand, from renders at 200 and 450 dpi. The second reading",
    "covered rows 1-11 of columns 1-4 and rows 21-26 of all five columns - 74 cells",
    "at both corners and the middle - and agreed with the first on every one.",
    "Any row that DISAGREES with the derivation is re-read at high zoom before it is",
    "adjudicated, which puts the verification effort where it can change an outcome."
  ],
